  "Bloc9": {
    "ID": "ID Photo",
    "ePhoto": "ePhoto Code",
    "codeEphoto": [
      {
        "texte_accordeon": "<p>You need to provide a <a href=\"https://www.smartphone-id.com/ephoto-ants/\">ephoto digital signature code</a> (or ePhoto code) for an online request on the ANTS website?</p>\n<p>It's very simple, go to the Smartphone-iD website: Application ID Photo and ephoto. Download the app, choose the document you need (Driving License, Residence Permit, DCEM, etc.). Then take your photo and your signature on your smartphone and it's done. After validation of your photo by our team of experts, you will receive your ePhoto code in your mailbox in a few minutes.</p>\n",
        "titre_accordeon": "How to obtain an ePhoto code?"
      }
    ],
    "photo_didentite": [
      {
        "texteAccordeon": "<p>If you apply with a paper application, an official passport photo for South Africa should be</p>\n<ul>\n<li>45 mm high and 35 mm wide,</li>\n<li>face size should be between 29mm and 34mm high (from the crown of your head to your chin).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>The face must occupy 70-80% of the photo height</b>, ensuring clear visibility of facial features.</p>\n<p>Ensure the face is evenly lit, with no shadows or reflections, and that it is clearly distinguishable from the background.</p>\n<p>For digital passport photos, the image resolution should be <b>600 dpi.</b></p>\n",
        "titre_accordeon": "What size is the passport photo for South Africa?"
      }
    ],
